{"consequencesIfNotApproved":"UE behavior will remain undefined when SSBs that the UE measures for L1-RSRP/SINR (and are not associated with the PCI that has active TCI states) overlap with UL channels/signals.","crCategory":"F","crNumber":"343.0","crRevision":"1.0","for":"Agreement","id":"tdoc:R1-2208084","reasonForChange":"For inter-cell mTRP in FeMIMO, the following has been agreed in RAN1#108-e:


In 38.213, the “active additional PCI” in the agreement is captured as the PCI associated with the active TCI states. However, this is problematic as UE still measures SSBs (L1 measurment) from the PCIs not associated with the active TCI states.
When SSBs that the UE measures for L1-RSRP/SINR (and are not associated with the PCI that has active TCI states) overlap with UL channels/signals, there is no procedure currently defined as to whether the UE should measure the SSB or transmit the UL channel/signal given that the UE is not capable of full-duplex operation in TDD.","reservationDate":"8/25/2022 7:25:44 AM","status":"agreed","summaryOfChange":"Remove the condition “associated to physical cell ID with active TCI states” in relevant sections.","tdocNumber":"R1-2208084","title":"CR on inter-cell mTRP when SSBs of additional PCI overlap with UL","tsgCRPack":"RP-222400","type":"CR","uploadedDate":"2022-08-28T18:21:16.803000"}

